{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>And the goat</b> — like its meaning: because Alexander died when his power grew strong, and in the days of his youth, about thirty years old, he died." "<b>And notable horns came up</b> — horns in the vision; this is that his kingdom was divided into four kings." "<b>Toward the four winds of heaven</b> — this is \"and four heads to the beast\"; the place of the kingdom for each of them: the first place Syria, and the second is Egypt, and the third the land of Israel, and the fourth the land of Persia; and so it is written in the books of the kings."], :book :daniel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Daniel - Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/daniel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:20:25.130664045Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}